STRATEGY ARTIFACTS & DELIVERABLES
Opportunity Memo
•	Core Concept: A short decision document that explains why an AI opportunity should or should not receive investment.
•	Key Details & Data: Cover pain, value, feasibility, risk, assumptions, and next-step recommendation.
•	Real-World Example: AI-assisted opportunity memo for a bank or retailer.
Value–Feasibility Matrix
•	Core Concept: A prioritization tool used to separate attractive AI opportunities from weak ones.
•	Key Details & Data: Value should capture urgency, workflow pull, and commercial upside. Feasibility should capture data readiness, trust risk, and integration load.
•	Real-World Example: Compare several bank AI opportunities before deciding which one receives investment.
Build–Buy–Partner Brief
•	Core Concept: Documents how the required AI capability should be sourced.
•	Key Details & Data: Assess market pull, data readiness, distribution, strategic importance, vendor dependency, and time-to-market.
•	Real-World Example: Decide whether to use an external AI API or develop an internal capability.
Roadmap Bet Sequencing
•	Core Concept: Strategy requires choosing what to do now, what to delay, and what to reject.
•	Key Details & Data: Not every attractive AI possibility deserves the next unit of investment or attention.
•	Real-World Example: A SaaS company can use a roadmap sequencing brief to prioritize competing AI initiatives.
________________________________________
HDFC BANK CASE — AI OPPORTUNITY MAPPING
HDFC Bank Customer-Service AI
•	Core Concept: AI strategy should prioritize opportunities rather than treating all potential AI use cases equally.
•	Key Details & Data: Possible areas include support automation, fraud triage, sales assistance, and knowledge retrieval. Selection depends on customer pain, risk, workflow fit, value, and feasibility.
•	Real-World Example: The case asks which banking opportunity should be prioritized, where APIs are sufficient, and which workflows should remain human-led.
⭐ Session 3 Takeaway
Good AI strategy is selective.
The PM should be willing to say:
BUILD NOW → DELAY → BUY/API → KEEP HUMAN-LED → REJECT
The goal is not a long list of AI ideas. The goal is a recommendation that leadership can fund or reject.
