TERMS TO MEMORIZE
•	AI Product: A product in which AI materially improves a user decision, workflow, or outcome.
•	Prediction Product: AI product that predicts or classifies an outcome.
•	Recommendation System: AI system that ranks or selects relevant options.
•	Generative AI Product: AI product that generates content or outputs within a workflow.
•	Hybrid AI Product: Product combining multiple AI modes.
•	Data Layer: Product-stack layer containing the data and signals needed by AI.
•	Model Layer: Layer that converts data into AI outputs.
•	API/Application Layer: Layer connecting AI capability to the product workflow.
•	UX Layer: Layer through which users interact with AI output.
•	Human-in-the-Loop: Design where humans review, approve, override, or escalate selected AI decisions.
•	Decision Rights: Explicit ownership of who decides, reviews, and escalates a trade-off.
•	AI Opportunity: Business or user problem where AI may materially improve the outcome.
•	Value–Feasibility Matrix: Framework comparing business value with execution feasibility.
•	Build–Buy–API: Decision about whether an AI capability should be internally developed or externally sourced.
•	Vendor Dependency: Reliance on an external provider for an important capability.
•	Core IP: Intellectual property strategically important enough to justify ownership.
•	Feature: Narrow capability solving a specific product problem.
•	Platform: Reusable capability supporting multiple workflows or use cases.
•	JTBD: Jobs-to-be-Done; the progress the customer is trying to achieve.
•	Opportunity Memo: Decision artifact explaining the value, feasibility, risk, and recommendation for an opportunity.
•	Data Readiness: Whether available data is sufficiently complete, reliable, fresh, and usable for the intended AI product.
•	Model Lift: Improvement produced by the model relative to an existing approach.
•	Time-to-Value: Time required before an AI initiative produces meaningful value.
•	Decision Artifact: Written output that makes a recommendation, trade-off, evidence, and next decision explicit.
