SESSION 4 — AI PRODUCT STRATEGY & OPPORTUNITY IDENTIFICATION – 2
Session 4 focuses on Product-Market Fit, platform strategy, recommendation logic, competitive positioning, and opportunity mapping.
Product-Market Fit for AI Products
•	Core Concept: AI Product-Market Fit (PMF) means the product creates repeatable, trusted, economically meaningful value, not just curiosity or initial usage.
•	Key Details & Data: Usage alone does not prove PMF. Look for repeat use, workflow dependence, willingness to pay, trust resilience, and behaviour after initial excitement fades. Reliability and trust are part of PMF.
•	Real-World Example: ChatGPT consumer adoption and GitHub Copilot developer retention show the difference between trial and sustained workflow value.
Novelty vs Real PMF
•	Core Concept: Novelty attracts users. PMF keeps them.
•	Key Details & Data: PR buzz, experimentation, downloads, or one-time exploration can create false PMF signals. Strong PMs separate novelty metrics from durable behavioural signals.
•	Real-World Example: The PDF asks students to compare ChatGPT adoption with GitHub Copilot retention patterns.
Quick Recall
Real AI PMF = Repeat Use + Workflow Dependence + Willingness to Pay + Trust
________________________________________
ChatGPT as a Platform Product
•	Core Concept: An AI product becomes platform-like when its value expands beyond one feature or workflow.
•	Key Details & Data: Evidence includes reuse across jobs, ecosystem participation, partner leverage, user habit formation, and extensibility beyond one task.
•	Real-World Example: ChatGPT plugins and ecosystem logic are compared with Salesforce/Microsoft layering AI across product suites.
Feature Trap vs Platform
•	Core Concept: Broad ambition alone does not make an AI product a platform.
•	Key Details & Data: A platform requires reusable workflows, ecosystem participation, developer or partner pull, expanding user dependence, and extensibility.
•	Real-World Example: Notion AI vs Microsoft Copilot shows how similar AI capabilities can occupy different positions in a workflow.
Workflow Breadth
•	Core Concept: AI should appear where it reduces the most important user friction.
•	Key Details & Data: The PM chooses whether AI should be an assistant, inline suggestion, background automation, or absent entirely.
•	Real-World Example: Notion AI and Microsoft Copilot demonstrate different approaches to embedding AI into workflows.
________________________________________
AMAZON-STYLE RECOMMENDATION LOGIC
Discovery and Basket Expansion 
•	Core Concept: Recommendation systems should improve discovery and influence useful customer behaviour.
•	Key Details & Data: Recommendations depend on reliable behavioural data. Data requirements should define event schema, consent, freshness, and downstream use.
•	Real-World Example: Amazon product recommendations use behavioural signals to support discovery and basket expansion.
Ranking and Personalization
•	Core Concept: Recommendation strategy is broader than simply producing the best ranking.
•	Key Details & Data: PMs must ask what business behaviour the system is optimizing. Important measures include engagement depth, conversion lift, basket size, retention impact, and trust.
•	Real-World Example: Amazon recommendations are compared with Spotify discovery and habit formation.
Relevance vs Diversity
•	Core Concept: Recommendation systems face a trade-off between showing highly relevant items and providing enough diversity for useful discovery.
•	Key Details & Data: More personalization is not automatically better. Recommendations should remain useful and trusted rather than intrusive.
•	Real-World Example: Amazon and Spotify illustrate different recommendation objectives.
Lifetime Value
•	Core Concept: Recommendations can affect long-term customer behaviour, not just immediate clicks.
•	Key Details & Data: Evaluate discovery, conversion, basket size, engagement depth, retention, and trust.
•	Real-World Example: Spotify recommendations can support discovery and habit formation, while Amazon recommendations can support discovery and basket expansion.
Exam Point
Recommendation strategy ≠ ranking accuracy alone.
It is about behaviour change + business value + trust.
