COMPETITIVE POSITIONING
Data Advantage
•	Core Concept: Proprietary, reliable, useful data can strengthen an AI product's competitive position.
•	Key Details & Data: Data advantage requires coverage, completeness, freshness, consent, and event quality. More data is not automatically better data.
•	Real-World Example: Spotify event instrumentation shows how product usage can generate valuable behavioural signals.
Workflow Embedding
•	Core Concept: AI becomes stronger competitively when it becomes embedded in an important user workflow.
•	Key Details & Data: The AI should reduce friction at the point where the user needs help. Workflow dependence can strengthen retention.
•	Real-World Example: Notion AI and Microsoft Copilot show different approaches to workflow integration.
Switching Costs and Differentiation
•	Core Concept: Competitive advantage can come from data, workflow fit, user habits, ecosystem integration, and switching costs.
•	Key Details & Data: Model capability alone may not create durable differentiation. PMs should identify which advantage competitors would struggle to reproduce.
•	Real-World Example: Platform products can deepen user dependence by expanding across workflows.
________________________________________
OPPORTUNITY MAPPING & STRATEGY SYNTHESIS
Opportunity Mapping
•	Core Concept: Opportunity mapping compares AI opportunities rather than approving every attractive AI idea.
•	Key Details & Data: Evaluate workflow pull, user pain, business value, trust, feasibility, differentiation, and evidence quality.
•	Real-World Example: Candidate AI opportunities can be compared before roadmap investment.
Strategy Synthesis
•	Core Concept: AI strategy should produce a clear product bet.
•	Key Details & Data: Strong strategy connects PMF + platform/feature choice + recommendation/business logic + competitive advantage.
•	Real-World Example: The session uses ChatGPT, Amazon, Spotify, GitHub Copilot, Notion AI, and Microsoft Copilot to show different strategic choices.
Session 4 Takeaway
AI excitement ≠ PMF.
Durable AI strategy requires:
Value → Repeat Use → Trust → Economics → Differentiation
